# Business Logic

All domain rules live in `src/lib/business/` as pure TypeScript functions — no I/O, no database access, no environment variables. This makes them trivially testable and prevents business logic leaking into pages or handlers.

## Module overview

```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph business["src/lib/business/"]
        age[age.ts\nAge rules + session dates]
        enq[enquiry.ts\nValidation + routing]
        book[booking.ts\nBooking validation + confirmation]
        tmpl[templates.ts\nTemplate rendering]
        tok[tokens.ts\nToken generation]
    end

    subgraph consumers
        API[API handlers]
        Pages[Astro pages]
        Email[Email senders]
    end

    API & Pages & Email --> age & enq & book & tmpl & tok
```

## age.ts

| Function | Returns | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `athleticsSeasonEndYear(dateIso)` | `number` | Calendar year of 31 Aug ending the season |
| `ageOnDate(dob, refDate)` | `number\|null` | Whole years on a reference date |
| `ageForAthletics(dob, sessionDate)` | `number\|null` | Age on 31 Aug of the relevant season |
| `resolveAgeGroup(dob, sessionDate, groups)` | `AgeGroupConfig\|null` | Matches athlete to age group from D1 list |
| `isAgeGroupEligible(dob, sessionDate, group)` | `boolean` | Validates athlete against a specific group |
| `getNextNSessionDates(ageGroup, n)` | `string[]` | Next N valid session dates for an age group |
| `validateSessionDate(dateIso, ageGroup)` | `boolean` | Date is future and valid for age group |
| `formatDateForDisplay(dateIso)` | `string` | `"Tuesday 14 April 2026"` |

## enquiry.ts

| Function | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `validateEnquiryData(data)` | Throws on invalid body — email format, DOB plausibility |
| `routeEnquiry(ageGroup)` | Returns `'taster'` or `'waitlist'` based on `booking_type` |
| `sanitiseString(value)` | Trims + collapses whitespace |

## booking.ts

| Function | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `validateBookingRequest(date, dob, ageGroup)` | Validates session date + age group eligibility |
| `buildBookingConfirmation(enquiry, booking, ageGroup, venue)` | Returns confirmation data including Google Calendar URL |
| `buildAvailabilityList(dates, bookedCounts, capacity)` | Availability array for booking page display |

## templates.ts

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    HTML["Template HTML\n{{contact_name}} booked for {{session_date}}"] --> Render[renderTemplate\nvars dict]
    Render -->|All vars provided| Output[Rendered HTML]
    Render -->|Missing var| Throw[Throws Error\nbefore any send]
```

| Function | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `renderTemplate(html, vars)` | Replaces `{{variable}}` — throws if any var is missing |
| `validateTemplateVariables(html, allowed)` | Returns unknown vars — used in admin editor |
| `extractTemplateVariables(html)` | Lists all `{{vars}}` found |
| `SAMPLE_TEMPLATE_VARS` | Default values for all known variables (used in preview) |

